# Local secrets for ./serve.sh and ./phone.sh. Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.
# Already-exported non-empty shell variables win; this file only fills gaps.
# A blank KEY= here does not block a later real value in .env or the shell.
# Never commit .env.

# Required for Feedback notes to reach GitHub (Issues: read and write on the repo).
MIDIMAN_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional — defaults are fine for peak-luli/midiman. Uncomment to override.
# MIDIMAN_FEEDBACK_REPO=peak-luli/midiman
# MIDIMAN_FEEDBACK_ISSUE=10
# MIDIMAN_FEEDBACK_LABEL=feedback
# Attachments host for the Learn screenshot (default uploads.github.com).
# Tests point this at a stub; you do not normally need to set it.
# MIDIMAN_GITHUB_UPLOAD=https://uploads.github.com

# Optional — after a note lands on GitHub, POST a small JSON ping to a Grok Bot
# routine so Miriam is notified. URL enables it; unset means no call (default).
# KEY is the routine's sender key, sent as Authorization: Bearer <key>.
# HEADER, if set, is the full Authorization value and wins over KEY
# (paste the trigger card's "Authorization: Bearer …" line here if you prefer).
# MIDIMAN_FEEDBACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# MIDIMAN_FEEDBACK_WEBHOOK_KEY=
# MIDIMAN_FEEDBACK_WEBHOOK_HEADER=
